1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Run your hand across your tire tread —
feel sharp on one side, smooth on the other?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
That saw-tooth feel is called feathering —
you have to feel for it, it won't just show up looking at it.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
One clue: it usually points to toe misalignment —
tires pointed slightly in or out instead of straight.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
But an alignment alone doesn't always fix it — a worn
tie rod end or bushing can cause the same wear.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Don't guess which one it is.
A quick check can point to the actual cause.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Worth checking before it eats through a new set of tires.
Stop by and we'll take a look. Nick's Tire & Auto.
